  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Dharmendra @ Lahari vs State Of U.P. on 1 October, 2019 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 78 Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 41130 of 2019 Applicant :- Dharmendra @ Lahari Opposite Party :- State Of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Gyanendra Kumar Singh Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Siddharth,J.",
    "facts": "Offence under sections 60(2) of Excise Act is bailable and trible by Magistrate. False recovery has been alleged. The applicant is languishing in jail since 30.08.2019, who is not a previous convict. On the other hand learned AGA has opposed the prayer for bail.",
    "arguments": "Keeping in view the nature of the offence, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, submissions of the learned counsel for the parties noted herein above, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another reported in (2018)3 SCC 22 and without expressing any opinion on the merits of Dharmendra @ Lahari vs State Of U.P. on 1 October, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/171475311/ 1",
